  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Inter-Faith Community Action Groups for Peace-building and Inclusive Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims at fostering dialogue, understanding, and collaboration among different religions and faith-based communities to enhance politicized-ethnic community dialogue; promote inclusive governance and peaceful co-existence through Inter-Faith Community Action Groups as Change Agents. The project will establish and strengthen inter-faith networks within the Inter-Religious Council of Sierra Leone at grassroots levels, across four (4) districts (Bombali, Port Loko, Bo and Kenema); identify women of faith aspiring for political leadership at both local and national levels, build their capacity and support them through.
This project focuses on empowering youth and women of Faith in the four regions through targeted capacity-building initiatives. Key areas of focus include governance, leadership, inclusive decision-making, gender equality and advocacy. These efforts are designed to enhance the ability of women and youth networks to participate actively in community decision-making, advocate for their rights, and improve their economic livelihoods.

Moreover, there is an extention of the project for one year and some new activities are added.</narrative>
  </description>
